{"title":"2018 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Longer)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Longer)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are externally tangent to each other and are internally tangent to a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> at points  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, as shown in the diagram. The distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/5/c85ea1ad780a799bdaf8f327e664f65eb6f3546b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"18\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1d7b33c122356459463ccf321031d04f8f53752.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),13)); draw(circle((5,-6.2),5)); draw(circle((-5,-6.2),5)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (9.5,-9.5), S); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (-9.5,-9.5), S); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51239b5dd3cf63b3daced7294839cc563d1dcb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }   21   \\qquad    \\textbf{(B) }  29   \\qquad    \\textbf{(C) }  58   \\qquad   \\textbf{(D) } 69 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }   93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f5cde9eec57d1be48c64499b92a5ed49bb52b18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),13)); draw(circle((5,-6.25),5)); draw(circle((-5,-6.25),5)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (-8.125,-10.15), S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (8.125,-10.15), S); draw((0,0)--(-8.125,-10.15)); draw((0,0)--(8.125,-10.15)); draw((-5,-6.25)--(5,-6.25)); draw((-8.125,-10.15)--(8.125,-10.15)); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, (0,0), N); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;, (-5,-6.25),NW); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;, (5,-6.25),NE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let the center of the surrounding circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The circle that is tangent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will have point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the center. Similarly, the circle that is tangent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> will have point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> as the center. Connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e35dd6d3c033f72a812728441ec7d87136db3c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XA$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/03933a7bd92d2cf64844a19ce10785a23f497959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XB$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" />. Now observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3039f01ba9e41f5490b7130e344be554015a25b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XYZ$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859d04abfad1da7b886d652c4ce7de207589dcd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XAB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> by SAS.\n</p><p>Writing out the ratios, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe2512bf29a8a348577f7d3ab0ac8bfd57152c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{XY}{XA}=\\frac{YZ}{AB} \\Rightarrow \\frac{13-5}{13}=\\frac{5+5}{AB} \\Rightarrow \\frac{8}{13}=\\frac{10}{AB} \\Rightarrow AB=\\frac{65}{4}.\\]\" width=\"453\" height=\"37\" />\nTherefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d46f24c31d8a834d3a48cec59b58b0a799f5079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65+4= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 69}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Longer.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Longer)\">Solution 2 (Longer)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Longer)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, let the center of the surrounding circle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, a tangent circle be tangent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and have point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as the center, and the other tangent circle be tangent at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and have point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> as the center (see the figure in Solution 1). We can deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/8046cd0ca54fb1d7f5b405a773c48a200e93adf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XY=XZ=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0ca7601737765110df0422f10d1291b419ab73d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Then, by the Law of Cosines, we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d586902a4d6041cb0bcfa517408a34462ac49db8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[YZ^2 = XY^2 + XZ^2 - 2(XY)(XZ)\\cos{\\angle YXZ} \\Rightarrow 100  =  64  +  64  -  2 (8) (8)\\cos{\\angle YXZ}\\]\" width=\"638\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d0ec7a5da7bf6aa6cc702282aed62aac261614.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow\\cos{\\angle YXZ}=\\frac{7}{32}\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now, notice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/6/256f221db556fa67d65a8597043fda2b3aab1d36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XA=XB=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" />. Further notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98e410f8ef66d3a591036df5c116f4185ce8b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YXZ=\\angle AXB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"141\" height=\"14\" />. Again, by the Law of Cosines,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa98438f40bcf8e97f16060b3bdec502846a8d0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AB^2 = XA^2 + XB^2 - 2(XA)(XB)\\cos{\\angle AXB}\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"20\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd85e006dbbb17110c6c485adf7d4bfef4eec4f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\Rightarrow AB = \\sqrt{169 + 169 - 2(13)(13)(\\frac{7}{32})} = \\frac{65}{4}\\]\" width=\"347\" height=\"43\" />\nThus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d46f24c31d8a834d3a48cec59b58b0a799f5079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$65+4= \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 69}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"141\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~RedKalkulus\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Interactive_Teaching_Approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=clcMXHuuIZU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=clcMXHuuIZU</a>\n</p><p>~MathkidsbyMax\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let the circle tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and that tangent at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> have center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Here we prove by contradiction that the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/31655517c48e177bce4015169f5924872298a35b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{OO_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> must be the point of tangency of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9b8faa8e1a07f3e03891e6ff76b16ed4f6583b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is not the point of tangency of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9b8faa8e1a07f3e03891e6ff76b16ed4f6583b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />. Furthermore, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/31655517c48e177bce4015169f5924872298a35b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{OO_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />. Then, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9b8faa8e1a07f3e03891e6ff76b16ed4f6583b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> be tangent at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c8a2d4dc4b2abe72940409c9d35b8e9aeaa7a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ATO_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> is a right angle, so if we continue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f74591db1d72c92e38759f43dc51f6ee1adfe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TO_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" /> to hit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/2/c828c0225d230b88cc0143849ffbe8be15215f9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ATI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> must intercept a semicircle. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> therefore has to be the intersection of the diameter through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />. We previously assumed that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> had to be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8cb2cb0363ca1d64220dabd15e07ca4051e97f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{OA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Clearly, however, if point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9b8faa8e1a07f3e03891e6ff76b16ed4f6583b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> will intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> at more than one point, and therefore will not be tangent, leading to a contradiction. \n</p><p>Therefore, we have proved that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/31655517c48e177bce4015169f5924872298a35b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{OO_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" />, is the point of tangency between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c748db2ab4a67c0aa0dace8827ba7cbc3a48aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/9/cf9b8faa8e1a07f3e03891e6ff76b16ed4f6583b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\odot O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> are collinear. Therefore, there exists a line through all three points. Likewise, we can perform the same proof on the circle tangent at B, and our solutions above are valid.\n</p><p><br />\n~LeonQS\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CREATIVELY!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CREATIVELY!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/xFnLbr-qt6I\">https://youtu.be/xFnLbr-qt6I</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HJALwsbHZXc\">https://youtu.be/HJALwsbHZXc</a>\n</p><p>- Whiz\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=llMgyOkjNgU&amp;list=PL-27w0UNlunxDTyowGrnvo_T7z92OCvpv&amp;index=3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=llMgyOkjNgU&amp;list=PL-27w0UNlunxDTyowGrnvo_T7z92OCvpv&amp;index=3</a> - amshah\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=1328\">https://youtu.be/NsQbhYfGh1Q?t=1328</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A\">2018 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2018 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\"